// A modulation nobody can date to one chord.
//
// Two phrases. The first is unambiguously in C major. The second arrives in G
// major. Between them stands an A minor triad, which is `vi` in C and `ii` in
// G — a pivot chord (OMT `051-modulation.md`), and the reason the boundary is
// a reading rather than a measurement: the change of key has already happened
// by the D major chord that follows, and has not yet happened at the C major
// chord before.
//
// What `musa analyze --kind tonal` should say about it:
//
//   - Two key regions. The first is C major; the second is G major, because
//     the F-sharp in bar 4 is outside every C collection. Both are candidates,
//     never facts, because more than one region survives.
//   - At the boundary, *both* a modulation candidate and a tonicization
//     candidate, with the OMT 051 criteria attached to each: the pivot
//     criterion is satisfied, the "holds to the end of the passage" criterion
//     is satisfied, and the "a cadence confirms it" criterion is not answered
//     by pitch alone. Duration decides nothing.
//   - Bar 3 read as `vi` in C major *and* as `ii` in G major, both candidates,
//     in the same report. That is the pivot, stated rather than resolved.
//   - Bar 4 read as `V/V` in C major as well as `V` in G major (OMT
//     `050-tonicization.md`), which is the same ambiguity one chord later.
//
// The cadence at the end is a perfect authentic cadence in G major on the
// evidence of pitch: root position, tonic on top. It is still a candidate,
// because a phrase ending is a formal fact and this reading sees only notes.
piece "Pivot Ambiguity" {
    composer "musa";

    tempo 1/4 = 72;
    meter 4/4;
    key c major;

    score {
        harmony {
            at 1:1 c;
            at 2:1 f;
            at 3:1 am;
            at 4:1 d;
            at 5:1 g;
            at 6:1 am;
            at 7:1 d7;
            at 8:1 g;
        }

        part piano {
            clef treble;

            voice upper {
                phrase "antecedent" {
                    | [e4 g4 c5]/1
                    | [f4 a4 c5]/1
                    | [e4 a4 c5]/1
                }
                phrase "consequent" {
                    | [f#4 a4 d5]/1
                    | [g4 b4 d5]/1
                    | [e4 a4 c5]/1
                    | [f#4 a4 c5]/1
                    | [b4 d5 g5]/1
                }
            }

            voice lower {
                | c3/1
                | f3/1
                | a3/1
                | d3/1
                | g3/1
                | a3/1
                | d3/1
                | g3/1
            }
        }
    }
}
